WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.932 --> 00:00:05.789
- Hi, everybody, and welcome to our preview of Capital One's "The Match: Champions for Change."

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:11.300
I'm Brian Anderson, your host, and joining us via Cisco Webex are four competitors this year.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.850
We've got the two Hall of Famers, Phil Mickelson and Charles Barkley.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.870
And the two future Hall of Famers, Peyton Manning and Stephen Curry.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.340
Guys, thanks for being with us.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:24.510
Looking forward to watching all of you play or maybe at least watching three of you play golf.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.692
Coming up, November 27, Friday after Thanksgiving.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:34.357
Gonna raise a lot of money, the primary beneficiary, HBCUs (historically Black colleges and universities).

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.609
And we're going to be providing a bunch of meals as well.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.785
We're already basically nearly six million dollars into the charitable contributions.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.810
We haven't even started yet. So this should be a lot of fun.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.009
I want to go around the horn here, talk to everybody really quick. Phil, I want to start with you.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:55.249
This is your third time around with The Match. You've been a part of all of them.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.121
Now we're going to your home course, a place you love so much you bought.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.869
Tell us about Stone Canyon.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:06.599
Tell us about your expectations for The Match. The third version, "Champions for Change."

00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:13.347
- As I look at Peyton, I can't help but be envious and jealous of the fact that he won the last match.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.454
And so I took it away from his partner's home course

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.769
and brought it to a course that I own and have a little bit of knowledge and understanding on

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.240
because I want the title back.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:33.040
And I upgraded my partner. I brought in Sir Charles, and I feel like we're ready to go.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:38.950
And Stone Canyon is this beautiful setting that's going to be challenging for players of Steph and Peyton's skill level.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.000
But I think Charles and I are going to be just fine on it.

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:46.904
- And you'll be playing for Jackson State.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:57.844
Charles. My first question to you is, why on earth would you leave that cushy booth gig next to me and Trevor Immelman and want to go play golf in this scenario, man?

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:01.819
I mean, I thought we had a good thing going there in Florida.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:08.300
- Well, let me tell you something. It’s an honor and a privilege to play with these three guys, first and foremost.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:18.660
And listen, we're gonna raise a lot of money for some great charities. But, you know, BA, I got to pick a little point with you.

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:22.860
You said, number one, I'm blessed to be in the Hall of Fame and Phil's in the Hall of Fame.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.819
How do you know Steph and Peyton gonna get in the Hall of Fame?

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.852
- Confident, man. Peyton's going in, in '21. I feel it in my bones.
He’s a voter.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.520
- We don't know that yet.
- Brian’s a voter.
- It’s gonna be a nail-biter on both of those guys.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.720
You just said they future Hall of Famers. I mean, you’re pretty presumptuous there.

00:02:45.729 --> 00:02:48.339
- You know, that's what we do. We don't stick with the facts in my line of work.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:53.340
We just kind of, we throw a lot of stuff out there, and just, you know, we make it up as we go.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:57.691
Who are you playing for in the event? Charles, give us your college.

00:02:59.182 --> 00:03:00.182
- I'm playing for Tuskegee.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.899
You know, BA, I'm really concerned about a lot of these schools.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:11.529
I've been involved with Morehouse and Clark in Atlanta. And Miles College and Alabama A&amp;M in Birmingham.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:16.210
And I just added Tuskegee to my portfolio. So I'm just excited, man.

00:03:16.747 --> 00:03:23.099
Cuz it's a little down the street from Auburn. So I've been there many times, and I can't wait to raise a ton of money for them.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.870
- Very cool. All right, Peyton, you're up next.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.602
So you're the defending champ. Phil mentioned that. You're trading Tiger Woods for Stephen Curry.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:40.689
Your expectation level coming in. I thought you, you played great in the last match in the driving rain.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.430
You and Stephen are pretty formidable. You two are the favorites right now, according to DraftKings.

00:03:47.479 --> 00:03:49.658
- Well, this would be our first time playing together.

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:55.759
Steph and I never played golf together, and like Phil said, he brought it to his home course

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:59.337
where he designed it, knows all the nuances, knows where to hit the ball.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:07.819
Steph and I are not going to have a caddy, so we are going to be totally on our own the entire time.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.309
I'm a little concerned about playing with Steph.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:18.919
Steph doesn't really know what alternate shot is because he never alternates who shoots on the court.

00:04:20.029 --> 00:04:25.125
He shoots every time. So am I going to get to play? I'm not sure. But you know what? I'm fine with that.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:30.713
If he wants to hit every shot, let's do it. Our chances are probably better if he does.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.069
But it's an honor to be back.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:40.459
It's an honor to be asked by Phil and all the people that started The Match to be a part of this.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.609
Raised 20 million dollars last time for COVID relief.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:50.057
And as you said, the beneficiaries are HBCUs this year, which is a tremendous cause.

00:04:50.094 --> 00:04:53.360
It's going to be fun to be a part of it again, to compete with Steph

00:04:53.361 --> 00:04:57.820
and to watch Phil do his craft and to try not to watch Charles.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:03.001
I think it will be a challenge for Steph and I to kind of block our vision as he's hitting.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.529
I think mentally that's the right way to approach it.

00:05:08.452 --> 00:05:13.790
- Peyton, tell us the three schools you're going to be playing for. Not just one. You're taking on three there in Louisiana.

00:05:15.269 --> 00:05:25.050
- Yes, splitting some of the money raised through this match to start scholarships for a deserving student at Lane College in Tennessee,

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.215
Southern of New Orleans, SUNO, as it's known as, in New Orleans and Grambling State University.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:40.920
So honored to partner with those three schools and to try to help a deserving student take a little burden off of him or her.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:46.810
- That’s outstanding. All right, Stephen, you're new to the game. We're glad you're here.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:51.309
Welcome to The Match family. You've been watching from afar.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:55.449
What made you want to be a part of this and participate?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:06:00.550
I think we're all excited to see how your game holds up with these other competitors.

00:06:02.839 --> 00:06:06.318
- Oh, yeah. I was watching The Match 2, just kind of taking it all in,

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:13.310
you know, watching Peyton just surprise everybody with his talent out there on the course.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:19.339
Phil, just trying to do whatever he could with his partner early in the round and keep him motivated.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:22.489
I feel like he's going to have to do a lot of that come next Friday.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.419
So he's got some reps. That's good.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:32.359
But you know how much I love golf, competing, you know, all over the country,

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:36.779
just trying to play as much as I can and raise awareness of how much I love the game.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:44.949
So this is a cool opportunity. I think I petitioned pretty hard sending out that tweet during The Match 2, like, “Hey, I want in,” and now we're here.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:51.579
So the one thing I am, you know, a little concerned about is Phil's intimidation strategies.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:56.930
I'm looking at his frame right now, and that's just ridiculous.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:07:00.244
And I don't know if he's trying to send subliminal messages to me and Peyton or if he's...

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.126
I have a bookshelf back here, but I got nothing on it.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:07.789
So, a missed opportunity. Missed opportunity.
- It needs to start early. It has to start early.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.155
- Stephen, I know who you’re representing. You started a golf school.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:16.242
Look at this. Look at what Coach [Samuel] Puryear sent me.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.795
- Yeah that's big right there. Howard Bison.

00:07:19.838 --> 00:07:22.410
-You're gonna play for them.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:25.999
- I am. I'm playing for Howard Bison.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:31.632
I was fortunate to be a part of bringing their Division I golf program back. Made that commitment last year.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:35.948
And obviously with COVID everything, things got a little bit delayed,

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.409
but we're looking forward to the spring to hopefully getting them out on the course,

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:42.700
and starting their journey as a program.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:46.189
And so we're playing for Howard, you know, Coach Puryear, who's there.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.679
We got a lot of talented men and women golfers that are in the program.

00:07:50.072 --> 00:07:56.899
Just try to create as many scholarships and lead towards an endowment that will keep the program around forever.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.820
So excited to play for them and hopefully raise a lot of money.

00:08:03.129 --> 00:08:05.665
- All right, well again, it's going to happen the Friday after Thanksgiving.

00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:11.742
Guys just want to bounce around a little bit with format. So it's going to be modified alternate shot on 17 of the 18 holes.

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:18.529
There will be a scramble hole. And that's going to be interesting.

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:25.630
So, Phil, you've kind of developed a little bit of the style of play. Now at The Match 2, the one we did on Memorial Day,

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:33.729
alternate shot was on the back nine. And you and Tom had a great run, had an amazing nine holes on that alternate shot.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:37.330
So maybe you tailor that a little bit to your game. You and Charles.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:42.609
I'm curious to see how much desert time you're going to get with Charles on the alternate shot format.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:49.509
- Well, I'm not unfamiliar with playing out of the rough, out of the desert, so that doesn't scare me off.

00:08:51.159 --> 00:08:56.759
My partner, he knows how to play the game.

00:08:56.770 --> 00:09:00.549
When I played with Charles first time back in the ‘90s when he was on the Phoenix Suns,

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:05.950
he shot in the 70s. Every round, he hit the ball solid with no issues whatsoever.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:14.279
And we're gonna dig deep and bring that game back. And I think we're going to win by kind of a large margin.

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:17.499
So my biggest concern is more I don't want it to end too early.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.299
Like, I don't want to close them out 6 and 5 and not make it interesting and exciting for the fans.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:26.049
So we certainly are concerned about that.

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:31.112
But, you know, from a game standpoint, my man can putt. My man can putt.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.149
He's got soft hands, a great touch on the greens.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:42.129
And if I can get the shots around the cactus and onto the green, we're going to be in good shape.

00:09:44.649 --> 00:09:49.500
- Charles, you got a membership there at Stone Canyon yet? I mean, how many practice rounds have you put in at this point?

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:53.384
- I've been there twice to practice.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:59.480
Get practice rounds in. And I'm going up one more time with the great Gary McCord,

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:04.299
one of my neighbors in Arizona. Cannot wait to get up there again.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:14.009
The guys up at Stone Canyon have been amazing. I played with Coach [Steve] Loy last week, so I'm really looking forward to it.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:19.940
Man, Imma have a great time. And I will say this, if I don't play well, I'll be very disappointed.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:28.090
I have hit balls for at least a minimum five hours a day, and I played every single day for the last month.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:35.270
If I don't play well, I'll be—number one—I'll be disappointed. Because I don't want to let Phil down.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:41.748
And listen, you know, Peyton, I just got to make sure he got my phone number. He used to text me all the time.

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:48.169
But since Tennessee hadn't won a game, it's been a few weeks since he texted me.

00:10:49.039 --> 00:10:54.710
- It's been more of a mental strategy by Steph and I not to text our opponents.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:57.512
We just wanted to kind of get our game faces on.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:04.100
And, you know, that's kind of news to me that Charles has played, has been to Stone Canyon three times.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:10.390
He hasn't played golf. He's just gone there to eat three times. They have great lunch and dinner service.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:14.652
So this will be his first time playing the course in the actual match on Friday.

00:11:16.669 --> 00:11:17.669
So I feel a little better with that.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:22.421
I think the one thing that didn't go unnoticed by me—I saw Steph kind of react—

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:26.860
is in Phil's opening comment saying that he upgraded his partner.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:31.879
Now, if I'm a certain quarterback down in Tampa, I don't know how to take that.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:36.229
You know, Charles, I know he's trying to create some confidence in his partner.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:41.840
But I mean, Charles, you know, in that cushy booth, rippin' on Tom.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:48.590
And now I can see Tom tweeting a little bit during this match, especially if Charles finds one of those,

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:55.040
finds a piece of desert or a cactus that he's by. I see a certain tweet coming out of one Tom Brady.

00:11:59.429 --> 00:12:03.599
- Tell us, Phil, a little bit about the course and where you think some of the strategy will come into play.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.760
I know there's a couple of drivable par fours.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.299
You guys are going to play different tees on some of the holes.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:12.790
And I think, Charles, they may just place him on the green a couple of times.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:17.252
Is that kind of how it's going to go down, or what's the plan for Charles on these really difficult holes?

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:22.590
- At Stone Canyon, we actually have Chuck Tees.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:31.679
Some people refer to them as ladies tees, but I call them Chuck Tees. They're up, you know, a little bit further up.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:40.520
But the course is actually pretty penalizing in spots because of the desert.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:45.971
But it's also got a great mixture of fun holes like drivable par fours, reachable par fives.

00:12:46.072 --> 00:12:48.946
Great mixture of length off the tee on the par threes.

00:12:48.974 --> 00:12:53.099
Our sixth hole is a spectacular par three with waterfalls and such.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:56.309
It's only about a wedge, but it's a very demanding shot.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:13:00.299
I actually feel like Charles is better adept on the green on that hole.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:07.980
So if I can hit the green and let him putt, that would be, that's our strategy on that.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.897
Same thing on the drivable par fours. We saw what happened in The Match 2,

00:13:10.898 --> 00:13:16.500
where we were really getting beat up pretty good. And then Tom and I on 11,

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:21.512
I drive the green and he rolls the putt in for eagle, and it just turns the whole match the other way.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:25.379
And we get all the momentum. And we really should have won that match.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:31.230
I mean, there were a couple of things down the stretch. I mean, Peyton's iron shot on 16 to three feet.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:36.019
I don't know. I don't know if that, that was legit or not. I don't know what happened there.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:41.279
I missed something. I couldn’t see the green. I couldn't see that far up the rain.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:46.440
And somehow his ball is three feet from the hole. When it's all said or done, I don't know, I question that.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:52.838
So I don't want to, you know, file lawsuits and try to, you know, question the outcome or any of that stuff.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.793
But I do have a question on that one.
- Yeah. No fraud involved.

00:13:58.063 --> 00:14:02.219
- So we are going to have spotters.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:06.419
I'm gonna to have spotters from my camp, make sure that any time we have a blind shot,

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:11.880
we're able to see the opponent, where the ball goes, tracking them in the desert, whatnot.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:20.027
But there's a great, there is a great mixture in all seriousness of spectacular clubs and shots throughout your bag.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:25.650
Like, you're not going to hit the same club over and over. And certainly with Charles as my partner, I won't either.

00:14:27.568 --> 00:14:31.768
- Stephen, I know you played with Phil in a pro-am on the PGA Tour. You've competed,

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:37.179
I think you competed as an amateur, but you played in what is now the Korn Ferry Tour.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.339
I mean, you've kind of been in the fire a little bit.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:43.539
And I know, Peyton, you've played in a number of pro-ams throughout your career.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:48.120
So give me, Stephen, give me a little idea of your mindset going into this event.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:51.460
You know, you're gonna be wearing a microphone, an earpiece.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:53.249
Gonna be a lot of banter going on.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.140
I know you can talk trash because I've heard it down on the floor.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:02.529
Are you going to be able to translate that with these alpha dogs and the golf game?

00:15:04.059 --> 00:15:04.719
- For sure.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:09.159
I mean, that's the benefit of playing, you know, in front of 19,000 people every day.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:12.580
You can handle noise and distractions even on the golf course.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.841
So bringing that element of experience.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.803
The one thing, I do have to ask about is,

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:22.995
you know, if there's a rules committee or board of governors or somebody that I can protest the spotters

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:27.879
that Phil is going to place on the course. That's like bringing your own refs to a playoff game.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.359
I don't understand how that works. So Peyton, we got to find, you know,

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:37.329
some eligible candidates to put it in the field ourselves, make sure, you know, we count all the strokes.

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:41.830
So that's big. But I think, yeah, I'm excited.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:45.399
Between me and Peyton, point guards and quarterbacks, there's a lot of chemistry

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:50.500
and a lot of similarities there of how we see, you know, a particular game, particular hole,

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:54.639
particular scenario and being able to kind of react on our feet.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.599
So, you know, hopefully we hit a lot of good shots.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:00.667
I've seen Peyton play, obviously, in The Match 2,

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.459
I know it's in there. Phil, that was not a coincidence.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:08.500
That's pure skill. So I'm ready to ride that train all the way to a victory.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:16.426
- Nice. Peyton, give me some thoughts about doing this again, second time around.

00:16:16.444 --> 00:16:21.959
How you enjoyed the first one you competed in, and then now

00:16:22.109 --> 00:16:25.200
we're here for the "Champions for Change" version of this one.

00:16:26.809 --> 00:16:32.869
- Well, my mindset is very similar. Is to try to put Steph in the best position.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.250
You know, when I was playing with Tiger,

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:39.940
trying to hit the best shot I could to give him just any chance of hitting it to the green.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:44.059
And so it's kind of the same approach with Steph. I haven't played with him, but I've seen his game.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:48.979
He's got all the shots, and I'm looking forward to kind of watching him do his thing.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:52.018
So hopefully I can drive the ball better than I did last time.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:17:00.529
And give him a chance to maybe to hit that second shot up there close to the hole for a little tap-in, tap-in birdie.

00:17:01.561 --> 00:17:08.929
The weather, Phil, as promised, will be better. It will not be a monsoon this time in Arizona.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:12.164
So that'll be good. I think there will be some blind shots all day

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:18.709
because it'll be hard to see around Charles where the ball went.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:24.610
So there will be some blind shots. Let's all just admit that.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:28.609
It's going to be a lot of fun. No question about that.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:35.809
Look, Phil Mickelson is one of the greatest competitors of all time. I can see the look in his eyes right now.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.433
He is focused. He is ready.

00:17:37.634 --> 00:17:46.336
How he thinks, you know, Charles is an upgrade. You know, I’d probably question Phil's GM skills on an NFL team.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:50.810
Like the Chargers this year, Brian. They're going to have a high pick in the draft. Right?

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.670
We pretty much know that. Right?

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:58.069
The idea is they're going to try to draft someone that's going to help them improve next year.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:03.230
And so for Phil to draft Charles, I'd like to know what went into that process,

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:09.049
what criteria he was looking for and how he landed Charles Barkley as his draft choice.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:11.490
- Go ahead, Phil.

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:16.939
- So that's actually an easy one to answer, because as I assess our opponents,

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:22.583
I find that Peyton, the thing that you do so well in golf is that you play within yourself.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:26.440
Like you know your limitations in golf. You don't try to play outside you.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:30.170
You hit solid shots, keep the ball in play and you advance forward.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:35.329
And I noticed in The Match 2, how you didn't try to get out of your element.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:40.309
And I noticed that when I played with Steph, he has a professional-caliber game.

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:44.944
He has all the shots, the ability to shape it each way. And we played on a tour-caliber course.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.339
I know the quality of our opponents.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:54.619
What I found, though, was, Peyton, is that the way to win is to get both of you out of your element.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:57.199
And there's nobody better at that than Charles.

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:02.382
He knows what to say and how to say it at the right time to get you out of your element.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:10.013
And I have a feeling, in fact, I know that you're going to try shots that you shouldn't.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.559
And that's how we're going to end up winning.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:17.479
We're going to have you mess up much more so than we're going to have to outperform.

00:19:21.089 --> 00:19:22.985
- I get it. I get that now. I get that.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:29.180
I think that'll be a challenge for Steph and I, not to listen and not to watch anything that Charles does.

00:19:32.579 --> 00:19:33.579
- Yeah.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.866
You know, Tom was very complimentary of you, Peyton.

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:40.410
He was very complimentary of Tiger. He was very, very nice throughout.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:46.839
He didn't intimidate. He wasn't trying to intimidate, didn’t try to, like, hit crazy drives or do anything.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:50.731
And so you felt very comfortable. You were relaxed, you played within yourself,

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:54.479
and you had a great day, and you ended up winning a close match, 1-up. Again,

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:59.220
I still question a couple of the shots and, you know, throughout the round, but

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:07.829
I know Charles is going to be, he's going to be more attacking, like a very subtle needle,

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:13.859
but again, at the right times. And he just knows how to get people uncomfortable.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:18.630
And it's that talent that he has that is going to give us the upper hand.

00:20:21.192 --> 00:20:23.900
- All right Charles, give you last word here. We're gonna...

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.438
Everybody can jump in, too, but I'm calling it the Chucknado.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.119
The Chucknado is coming.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:33.449
Gary McCord, Trevor Immelman, they said your game is tight.

00:20:34.799 --> 00:20:39.454
- Peyton has been killing me today. I just can't wait till Friday cuz I'm going to play well.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:47.020
Me and my partner gonna ham and egg it. We're going to play fantastic.

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:51.809
I want these guys to go to the golf dictionary and look up the word “dormie.”

00:20:54.060 --> 00:21:01.229
Get used to that word dormie. So you'll probably be dormie around 14,

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:05.880
if we play, if we bring our A-game, if I bring my, my decent game.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:10.039
You guys get used to the word. You guys gonna be dormie around 14.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.239
Go look up what that means, dormie.

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:16.838
- That big word you used, "if," man.

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:19.740
We're not even going to be able to hear your trash talk from the Chuck Tees, though,

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:23.272
so it's not even going to make a difference. We’re like, “We can’t hear you way up there.

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:25.519
What are you even saying?”

00:21:28.889 --> 00:21:31.020
- Awesome, man. I can't wait to get this going.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.699
Appreciate everybody being a part of this one.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.779
We had great fun. The last two have been outstanding.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:39.684
Everybody's gonna be wearing microphones. We'll have cool technology.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:45.160
And we can't wait to see you guys perform and entertain, and we're all looking forward to it.

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:50.249
Thanks for doing this for us. And we'll see you guys on the golf course day after Thanksgiving.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.280
Appreciate it.

00:21:52.709 --> 00:21:53.458
- Yes, sir.

00:21:53.459 --> 00:21:54.709
- Thank you, thank you, thank you.

